WEBVTT

NOTE
Kid-friendly read-along for silent hand-drawn animation.
Short lines, about 4–8 sec display time. Retime in Aegisub to match video.
Add cues if your cut runs past ~4 min. UTF-8, LF, no BOM.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:10.000
A big giant named Goliath was mean.
He scared God's people!

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Goliath shouted, "Fight me!"
Everyone was afraid.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Young David heard the giant.
David trusted God.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
David said, "God will help me!"
He picked five smooth stones.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:52.000
David put one stone in his sling.
He prayed and ran forward.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:04.000
David swung the sling hard!
The stone flew fast!

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:16.000
The stone hit Goliath—BOOM!
The giant fell down!

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Goliath was defeated!
The bad army ran away.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:40.000
God's people cheered loud!
David won with God's help.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:52.000
God is stronger than any giant.
He helps us in every battle!

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:08.000
And all this assembly shall know that the LORD saveth not with sword and spear:

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:26.000
for the battle is the LORD'S, and he will give you into our hands.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:42.000
1 Samuel 17:47 (KJV)

NOTE
End verse cues: hold longer in Aegisub if kids need more read time. Nudge all times to your MP4.
